    {
      "id": "b29f9d573e3a92263dc55693ca61b7e322584542",
      "tag": "autogenerated:ai-review",
      "author": {
        "_account_id": 1345,
        "name": "Gerrit AI review for Lustre",
        "display_name": "AI review",
        "email": "gaireview@linuxhacker.ru",
        "username": "aireview",
        "status": "Contact Oleg Drokin (green@whamcloud.com) with any questions on this account"
      },
      "date": "2026-09-06 02:53:25.000000000",
      "message": "Patch Set 1:\n\n(1 comment)\n\nAI code review results below, please doublecheck\n\nLooks good. The restored counter names, config flags and sampling points match the pre-folio ones exactly (checked against d9b67be7148d), the order-0 claim holds since get_folio_create() maps to __filemap_get_folio() with no order bits, and the Fixes: tag resolves and quotes the right subject. One optional suggestion inline; no need to re-spin for it.\n\nSince the premise of the patch is that a rename silently removed a counter name that consumers parse, would a small regression test be worth adding? Something in sanity.sh that does a little IO and then checks osd-ldiskfs.*.stats still lists get_page and get_page_failures would have failed before this patch and passes after, and would catch the same class of breakage next time.",
      "accounts_in_message": [],
      "_revision_number": 1
    },
